      "id": "claim_82dfbaaa09844bad9ee3fa2c3644deef",
      "statement": "The numpy-financial library provides a core set of financial functions, including fv, pv, pmt, nper, rate, ipmt, ppmt, npv, irr, mirr, and simple_interest, which mirror common spreadsheet financial formulas and are implemented to support vectorized NumPy-style operations. High-level logic and input handling reside in _financial.py, while performance-critical numerical computations are offloaded to the _cfinancial.pyx Cython extension.",
