    {
      "id": "claim_a079802048bd4bdb881702aa5c1d8310",
      "statement": "Financial functions in numpy-financial are designed to behave like NumPy ufuncs, leveraging broadcasting to perform vectorized computations across compatible input shapes, and delegating heavy numerical computations to internal C-extensions (e.g., _cfinancial). Functions also incorporate custom error handling for financial mathematical edge cases via NoRealSolutionError and IterationsExceededError.",
